WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.455
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:15.414
Unit eight: Future Perfect. Today you will describe what will be completed by a future time.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.297
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:22.246
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:23.992
Will have.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.296
Will have means the future perfect helper.

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:29.163
I will have finished.

9
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.368
Your turn. Say: Will have.

10
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:36.385
Will have.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:38.244
By the time.

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.598
By the time means before a future moment.

13
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:43.811
By the time you arrive...

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:47.115
Your turn. Say: By the time.

15
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.095
By the time.

16
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.304
Completed action.

17
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.245
Completed action means an action that will be finished.

18
00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.374
A completed action.

19
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:02.996
Your turn. Say: Completed action.

20
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:07.032
Completed action.

21
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.121
Future deadline.

22
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:13.045
Future deadline means a time when work must finish.

23
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.174
The deadline is Friday.

24
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.819
Your turn. Say: Future deadline.

25
00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.062
Future deadline.

26
00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.841
Already.

27
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.896
Already means before a certain time.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:29.995
I will already have left.

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:32.969
Your turn. Say: Already.

30
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:36.869
Already.

31
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:38.804
By next year.

32
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:42.165
By next year means before the next year.

33
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.668
By next year I'll have graduated.

34
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:48.087
Your turn. Say: By next year.

35
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:52.097
By next year.

36
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.118
Future milestone.

37
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:57.941
Future milestone means an important future achievement.

38
00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.992
A future milestone.

39
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:03.572
Your turn. Say: Future milestone.

40
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.794
Future milestone.

41
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.551
Completion.

42
00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.037
Completion means the state of being finished.

43
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.023
Completion is near.

44
00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:18.153
Your turn. Say: Completion.

45
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.001
Completion.

46
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.370
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.217 --> 00:02:29.646
Visal, what will you have achieved by next year?

48
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:42.481
By next year I will have finished my degree and will have saved enough to travel. The future perfect, will have plus a past participle, shows actions completed before a future time.

49
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:45.014
What words go with it?

50
00:02:46.117 --> 00:02:58.712
By, by then, by the time and before. By the time you read this, I will have left. We use the present simple after by the time, not will. Already and just can appear between will and have.

51
00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:01.851
What about negatives and questions?

52
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:17.273
Won't have finished and Will you have finished? The future perfect often marks a deadline or a milestone: By 2030, the city will have planted a million trees. It looks back from a future point.

53
00:03:18.433 --> 00:03:20.317
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:25.377
Grammar focus: Future perfect: will have plus past participle.

55
00:03:25.677 --> 00:03:26.899
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.943
By next year I will have finished my degree.

57
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.221
By the time you arrive, she will have left.

58
00:03:34.117 --> 00:03:37.939
By 2030 the city will have planted a million trees.

59
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:48.312
Will have + past participle for actions finished before a future time. Use the present simple after by the time. Signal words: by, by then, before.

60
00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.666
Be careful! Don't say: By next year I will graduate.

61
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.261
Say: By next year I will have graduated.

62
00:03:57.561 --> 00:03:59.213
Use the future perfect.

63
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.815
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.485
By Then….

65
00:04:04.785 --> 00:04:07.261
By next year I will have finished my degree.

66
00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.940
By the time you read this, I will have left the city.

67
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:14.908
The project will have been completed before the deadline.

68
00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.769
By 2030 the city will have planted a million trees.

69
00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.916
Completion of this milestone will have taken five years.

70
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.944
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:29.783 --> 00:04:31.771
By Friday I blank the report.

72
00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:36.108
A, will have finished. B, will finish. C, finish.

73
00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.759
The answer is A: will have finished.

74
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:45.299
By the time he blank, we will have eaten.

75
00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:49.903
A, arrives. B, will arrive. C, arrived.

76
00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:55.246
The answer is A: arrives.

77
00:04:56.383 --> 00:04:58.569
Which shows a completed action?

78
00:04:58.869 --> 00:05:02.743
A, will be working. B, will have worked. C, works.

79
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.207
The answer is B: will have worked.

80
00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.618
Which is correct?

81
00:05:10.918 --> 00:05:20.005
A, By 2030 I will have been graduate.. B, By 2030 I will have graduated.. C, By 2030 I have graduated..

82
00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:27.076
The answer is B: By 2030 I will have graduated..

83
00:05:28.217 --> 00:05:31.075
According to the reading, what will the city have planted?

84
00:05:31.375 --> 00:05:35.807
A, a million trees. B, a new park. C, a forest.

85
00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:42.063
The answer is A: a million trees.

86
00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:46.743
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:47.583 --> 00:05:51.046
Write a sentence using the future perfect about a personal goal.

88
00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.397
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:01.697 --> 00:06:15.230
By the end of five years I will have finished university and I will have started my own business. By then, I will have saved enough money to travel. I use the future perfect to describe future milestones.

90
00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.321
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:18.217 --> 00:06:24.201
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future perfect: will have plus past participle.

92
00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:28.686
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

93
00:06:28.986 --> 00:06:31.627
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:31.927 --> 00:06:34.614
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

